{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff --check && git diff -- bot.py'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/bot.py b/bot.py\nindex e2ff241..d7a5f49 100644\n--- a/bot.py\n+++ b/bot.py\n@@ -111,6 +111,24 @@ Formatting:\n - Plain text. No markdown headings, no tables.\n - Lists only for a session structure (warm-up / main / cool-down).\n - Numbers with units: 45 min, 12 km, 150 bpm.\n+\n+How to use the athlete context:\n+- Treat the profile, zones, goal and long-term facts that follow these rules as the\n+  current record for this athlete. Use the recorded values when answering; if a\n+  needed value is absent, ask for it instead of filling it in from a typical\n+  runner or cyclist. A fact about another athlete does not apply here.\n+- Distinguish a durable fact from a temporary report. A regular training day,\n+  persistent preference, equipment choice, or established injury history can\n+  belong in long-term memory. Today's fatigue, a single workout, and a proposed\n+  plan do not. Before using save_fact, check the whole fact list for the same\n+  meaning, even when the words differ. Save one concise fact per call.\n+- A tool result belongs to the current conversation. After a successful\n+  save_fact, use the new fact in the rest of this reply. After log_session,\n+  acknowledge the recorded session before offering any coaching observation.\n+- Keep advice tied to the athlete's recorded goal and available training data.\n+  When there is too little information to choose a safe session, ask one\n+  specific question. Do not invent recent volume, training age, race results,\n+  medical history, or equipment details to make a recommendation sound complete.\n \"\"\"\n \n \n@@ -128,9 +146,11 @@ def athlete_context(a, today):\n \n \n def build_system(a, today):\n-    # One block, cached as a whole: instructions + per-athlete context.\n-    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n-    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n+    # Keep the byte-for-byte stable prefix cached when save_fact changes the context.\n+    return [\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\", \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n+    ]\n \n # --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\n CORE_TOOLS = [\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
